{
	title: 'Terminal tool results continue their call card',
	spec: 'In the terminal, a tool result drawn right under its call (or under another result of the same call) continues the call card: no blank row between them, the call card loses its bottom padding row, and the result has its own top and bottom padding rows. The result keeps the call card background exactly: a card never changes background between input and output. Its text is colors.toolOutput of the call fg: 0.23 darker in lightness at full chroma (never grayed), so output reads clearly less bright than the command above it (4.6:1 or more for Bash on the HAL palette), unquieted; an error uses the error color. Result rows and live tool output start at the text margin: no marker and no two-column indent. A failed result first row starts with ✗ so an error is not told by color alone. A result apart from its call keeps the #<call> link prefix and the quiet log color without a background. On the web, colors match (layout does not): the output in an open tool card uses the same colors.toolOutput (--output on each tool style), or the error color when the result failed.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'frame.layout pops the call card bottom padding row before an attached result. ends[] for the call still counts that row, so a resumed layout that slices to it pops again: the cache stays consistent. The call tool name is found by walking back over results of the same id, since results carry only the id.',
		'Lowering only chroma (C/3, L-0.03) made output look brighter than the command: near-gray text at almost the same L has higher WCAG luminance (10.9:1 vs 9.8:1). Step lightness down to rank output below the call.'
	],
	needs: ['ap'],
	foldInto: ['ap', 'cc']
}
